@0    = ~Hey you! What you doin' out of cage? Get back in cage now!~
@1    = ~Go away before I step on you.~
@2    = ~Die!~
@3    = ~You not talk like that to great Weenug! Weenug is famous as great fighter. Now go back in cage before I kick your arse!~
@4    = ~You a great fighter? Ha ha ha! What makes you so great at fighting?~
@5    = ~Oh great another short person with delusions of greatness. If I may ask, why do you think you're such a great fighter?~
@6    = ~I am great cause my granddad was great wizard. He could cast powerful spells and train dumb humans in the magic art. His smarts pass down to me. I know little magic but know more about fighting. Now go back in cage!~
@7    = ~Yeah right! A turnip has more intelligence than you do. Now move along before I hurt you.~
@8    = ~Well lets see those *fighting* skills of yours.~
@9    = ~You imbred <PRO_RACE>! I very smart and good fighter! You not go back in cage now. You be dead and I will have your ears for a necklace!~
@10   = ~Aye, Thorin, let me gut 'em. Me hammer be itchin' fer some blood!~
@11   = ~I just thought about that other group down here wandering around. They may hear us take out these sorry sods.~
@12   = ~Tor, now understand this. We kill these sods first, then we will go kill the other sods, ye understand?~
@13   = ~Ughhhhhhhhhhhh...~
@14   = ~Ughhh hehehehehehe ughhhh...~
@15   = ~Arggghhhh huhhhhhh?~
@16   = ~Urgghhh yeahhhhhh!~
@17   = ~Eh whats this? Who ye be? Ye dare disturb the Hammer Brothers three. Now we be takin' gold from ye. Hand it over and be quick or or we be crushin' ye like a tick.~
@18   = ~Who let you guys out of your cage? I think you have been down here sniffing the fumes far too long. We are not giving you any gold.~
@19   = ~Har har die ye bleedin' fools!~
@20   = ~I be Thorin mightest of all dwarves, this be Thurm and over there be Tor. Tor not say much, he had a granite slab dropped on his head when he was a babe.~
@21   = ~Shut yer trap, Tor, I dinnae ask fer yer comment. Mayhaps that be a good idea Thurm. No one will hear 'em scream down here.~
@22   = ~I nay worry 'bout that sorry lot, we kin wipe them out next.~
@23   = ~Now that be cleared up, time ta make rat food of these fools!~
@24   = ~Eh? What do you want?~
@25   = ~We want the magical tome you took from the Priest of Mystra.~
@26   = ~Nothing.~
@27   = ~That weak priest from a weak god hired you? You're not getting anything but our blades in your gut!~
@28   = ~Good get lost.~
@29   = ~Sheep haven't been putting out lately.~ [FARME04]
@30   = ~I love my sheep. They says a man's best friend is a dog. Nonsense I says! Sheep is a man's best friend.~
@31   = ~Sheep are mighty fine and so soft. I like their softness, it feels nice against my skin.~
@32   = ~What I do in my barn is my business. Don't listen to those lies others spread about me.~
@33   = ~I think my neighbor needs a favor from you. Go talk to him now and let me go back to petting my sheep.~
@34   = ~Heya! I was wonderin if ya could help me out with somethin.~
@35   = ~We might be able to help you, what is the problem?~
@36   = ~Sorry, we do not have the time.~
@37   = ~Well there be a fine book that I wanna read called Umar Witch Project Journal. The problem is I can't go into the inn on the account I owe that innkeeper a large amount of coin from my bar tab. Kin ya help me?~
@38   = ~Sure we can help out. Is this going to cost me any coin?~
@39   = ~Well thanks anyway, return if you change your mind.~
@40   = ~Nah. He has some in his storage. Just grab one and bring it to me.~
@41   = ~We'll get the book for you and return with it.~
@42   = ~I see you have returned. Did get that fine book fer me?~
@43   = ~No we did not. We'll go get it now.~
@44   = ~Please get it and return when you have it.~
@45   = ~You return and have that fine book! I'm most grateful for this. I shall give you 10 gold for the effort you put in to get it. A lot cheaper I may add compared to my bar tab of 800 gold pieces.~
@46   = ~Glad to see you again good <SIRMAAM>. I thank you once again in gettin this book fer me.~
